{
  "summary": "Vendors an experimental batch verification module in libsecp256k1 and integrates Schnorr signature batch verification into block validation. In both single-threaded and parallel script check queues, signatures that miss the signature cache are collected into a batch and verified simultaneously via multi-scalar multiplication before a block is accepted.",
  "problem": "Schnorr signatures in Taproot inputs are verified individually during block validation. Validating signatures one by one incurs full per-signature cryptographic verification overhead rather than leveraging the significant CPU speedup available from BIP 340 batch verification.",
  "evidence": [
    "secp256k1 batch benchmarks in src/secp256k1/doc/speedup-batch/bench_output.txt and speedup graphs show up to 2x or greater verification speedups when batching Schnorr signatures compared to individual verification.",
    "PR description notes this is a draft implementation intended for 'conceptual discussion, and collaborative benchmarking' while secp256k1 batch verification is under upstream review."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The PR vendors unmerged upstream secp256k1 work (secp256k1 PRs #1134 and #1789) directly into the src/secp256k1 subtree, accounting for most of the diff size.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased the vendored secp256k1 batch verification module to reflect recent upstream API changes (such as void add functions and context resetting), added a functional test for invalid Taproot output keys, and updated fuzz testing for the checkqueue.",
  "card": "This pull request integrates BIP 340 Schnorr signature batch verification into block validation using an experimental secp256k1 batch module. Taproot Schnorr signatures are currently checked individually, missing the mathematical performance gains of batch verification during block connection and initial block download. Vendored benchmarks demonstrate substantial speedups over individual verification as batch sizes grow. The change depends conceptually on upstream secp256k1 PRs #1134 and #1789.",
  "needs": [
    "rest_of_diff"
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "high",
    "touches": [
      "consensus",
      "validation"
    ],
    "why": "A flaw in batch scalar arithmetic or batch queue logic could incorrectly validate invalid signatures or reject valid blocks, causing consensus divergences or remote validation failures."
  }
}
